      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OCR Provider**\n\nI've decided to use the Google Cloud Vision API for OCR tasks in `extract_text.py`. The next step is integrating the API key securely and configuring the code to identify and utilize Google's service specifically. I will focus on modularity to facilitate future provider switches.\n\n\n**Implementing OCR Logic**\n\nNow I'm focusing on the actual implementation within `extract_text.py`. I'll start by incorporating the Google Cloud Vision API setup, including imports and client initialization. The core logic will center around parsing a command-line image path to feed into the API. I'm aiming for clean and modular structure.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863751308,
          "start": 1789863748938
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc31654a001RUqCurAjCpFsAU",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc316097001BQQIvWVcVHjJJN",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ce9fe8ffeK6N0jqu7uCuj3D",
      "time_created": 1789863748938,
      "time_updated": 1789863751308
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "grrYUzlwlrolscqj",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport sys\nfrom google.cloud import vision\n\ndef extract_text_from_image(image_path):\n    \"\"\"Extracts plain text from a scanned document image using Google Cloud Vision API.\"\"\"\n\n    # Instantiates a client\n    client = vision.ImageAnnotatorClient()\n\n    # Loads the image into memory\n    with open(image_path, 'rb') as image_file:\n        content = image_file.read()\n\n    image = vision.Image(content=content)\n\n    # Performs document text detection\n    response = client.document_text_detection(image=image)\n    texts = response.full_text_annotation\n\n    return texts.text\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python extract_text.py <image_path>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    image_file_path = sys.argv[1]\n    \n    # Set the GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable\n    # os.environ[\"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS\"] = \"/path/to/your/keyfile.json\" \n    # Replace with the actual path to your Google Cloud service account key file\n    \n    # You should have GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable set or \n    # pass the credentials explicitly in a production environment.\n    # For local development, you might need to set the environment variable:\n    # export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=\"/path/to/your/keyfile.json\"\n\n    try:\n        extracted_text = extract_text_from_image(image_file_path)\n        print(\"Extracted Text:\")\n        print(extracted_text)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "extract_text.py"
          },
